{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":115052,"duration_api_ms":115007,"num_turns":21,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cb1c4de0-5916-4039-acbe-e893da294dff","total_cost_usd":0.571183,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":43078,"cache_read_input_tokens":340341,"output_tokens":5269,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":43078,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":5269,"cacheReadInputTokens":340341,"cacheCreationInputTokens":43078,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.571183,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept the three documentation/metadata improvements (colonizable_area_factor note, pKa1 reference value, new shrimp param_meta). Reject the two amendments whose factual premises are incorrect: temp_condition divisors are validated in the >0.0 bucket not <=1.0, and NH3 stress does reach molt_stress_index indirectly through the condition pathway.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-8014730a","decision":"accept","rationale":"The valid_range upper bound of 1.1 in coarse_porous.toml allows colonizable_area_factor to exceed 1.0, but the param_meta.notes field does not explain why this is physically meaningful. For porous media, internal void surface area can legitimately exceed projected footprint area, but this should be stated explicitly. Adding a brief note (or tightening to 1.0 if the intent was different) prevents future confusion about the semantic meaning of the factor."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-d7c5dd73","decision":"accept","rationale":"In PROVENANCE_STATUS.md line 91, PKA2 is presented as a single 25°C value (10.33) with a note about the simplification. In contrast, pKa1(T) at line 90 only shows the Harned & Davis formula with no reference value. Adding ≈6.35 at 25°C alongside the formula would make cross-referencing against standard carbonate tables faster and bring formatting consistency with PKA2. This is a safe, documentation-only improvement."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-1c025102","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's premise is factually wrong. Inspecting presets.rs, temp_condition_low_divisor_c (line 997) and temp_condition_high_divisor_c (line 1001) are in the positive-value validator bucket (lines 980-1041, which checks `value <= 0.0`), not in the <=1.0 bucket (lines 1048-1154, which checks `value > 1.0`). The shipped values of 10.0 and 8.0 pass the >0.0 check without issue. The default shrimp preset is not rejected by this validation."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-f229f75f","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment correctly observes that hourly_pressure (line 506-507) only includes heat and instability accumulators, not NH3. However, nh3_stress_response_scale does reach the molt-stress pathway through an indirect but real chain: hourly_nh3_stress_accum → stress_penalty (line 433) → condition target reduction → condition_stress (line 495-497) → stress_pressure (line 513-517) → molt_stress_index. It also directly enters stress_total in compute_mortality_probabilities (line 1238). The doc comment at biology.rs:432-435 saying it routes into 'mortality and molt-stress channels' is imprecise about the indirection but not functionally wrong — changing nh3_stress_response_scale does change both mortality rates and molt stress outcomes."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7893222b","decision":"accept","rationale":"The param_meta section starting at neocaridina_davidi.toml line 102 has detailed provenance entries for other parameters but none for the six newly introduced tunables (temp_condition_low_divisor_c, temp_condition_high_divisor_c, molt_stress_condition_midpoint, molt_stress_thermal_cap, nh3_stress_threshold_mg_n_per_l, nh3_stress_response_scale). These are first-class scientific knobs exposed in the TOML — they need provenance/confidence annotations or at minimum explicit provisional/TODO markers to match the repository's documented expectations for parameter auditability."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f7581af4-b01c-4c30-8fbd-4fdb3d2a9566"}
